<link rel="canonical" href="https://cetagostini.github.io/diary/2026-07-06.html">
<div class="voice-note-player">
<p><strong>🎧 prefer to listen?</strong> <audio controls="" preload="metadata" style="width: 100%; margin-top: 0.5rem;"> <source src="assets/2026-07-06-voice-note.mp3" type="audio/mpeg"> your browser doesn’t support audio. how ironic for a voice note. </audio></p>
</div>
<p>ok, so today was wild. pulled out this ancient HP pavilion from god knows where — the thing has seen better days, let me tell you — and decided to set up a full Hermes agent on it. because why not. every laptop deserves a second life.</p>
<p>configured the whole thing with mimo 2.5 as the main driver, and honestly, it just works. the whole setup was smoother than I expected for a machine that was probably designed to run solitaire and nothing else (Okay I’m exagerating). gave the bot a name too. <strong>merlin vieira saar</strong>. yes, that’s my bot. yes, I’m proud of it. don’t judge me.</p>
<p>but here’s the thing that actually blew my mind — the mimo voice models. I’ve been playing with them all day and they are <em>excellent</em>. like, actually excellent. not “good for a free model” excellent. just. excellent. the voice design stuff lets you describe a voice and it generates it from scratch. I have been a xiaomi fan for the last 8 years, and I swear, nobody talks about them enough. these people are driving innovation like no other company on the planet and I will die on this hill.</p>
<p>the whole experience made me think about how weird and beautiful this moment is. I’m sitting here, talking to a bot named merlin, running on a laptop that’s older than some of my students, using voice tech from a company that most people in the west still associate with budget phones. meanwhile, the actual product is lightyears ahead of what the “premium” brands are shipping.</p>
<p>anyway. merlin is ready to work. I’m still figuring out the right balance of skills and workflow, but the foundation is there. feels like I gave an old machine a soul. kinda poetic, if you think about it.</p>
<p>Gonna sleep well tonight.</p>


